&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;Income taxes are accrued in accordance with the FERC Policy Statement on Income Tax Allowance permitting the accrual of income taxes on a pass-through entity and the associated taxes accrued are treated as deemed contributions from the owners, whereas net operating loss carryovers are treated as deemed distributions. The deemed contribution recorded was $2.3 million in 2025 and $2.9 million in 2024 and was included within Other Paid-in Capital in the Comparative Balance Sheet. We will make all necessary adjustments to account balances upon a ruling in Docket No. AC18-220-000. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;On December 22, 2017, the United States enacted the &amp;#8220;Tax Cuts and Jobs Act&amp;#8221; (&amp;#8220;TCJA &amp;#8221;). The changes in the TCJA are effective for taxation years beginning after December 31, 2017. While the changes are broad and complex, the most significant change is the reduction in the corporate federal income tax rate from 35% to 21%. We recorded a $8.2 million decrease to our 2017 deferred income tax liability, a $2.9 million increase to our 2017 deferred income tax asset and an offsetting increase of $11.1 million to our regulatory liability. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;In 2018 pursuant to guidance established in FERC Docket No. PL19-2-000, we began amortizing the regulated liability utilizing the reverse South Georgia flowback methodology over the 30.5 year remaining life of the assets. In 2025, we recorded a $0.4 million decrease to regulatory liability, a $0.1 million decrease to our 2025 deferred income tax asset and an offsetting $0.3 million benefit to our 2025 deferred federal tax expense. In 2024, we recorded a $0.4 million decrease to regulatory liability, a $0.1 million decrease to our 2024 deferred income tax asset and an offsetting $0.3 million benefit to our 2024 deferred federal tax expense.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style="mso-element: para-border-div; border: none; border-left: none windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-left-alt: none windowtext 0in; padding: 0in 0in 0in .25in;"&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: .25in; text-indent: -.25in; border: none; mso-border-left-alt: none windowtext 0in; padding: 0in; mso-padding-alt: 0in 0in 0in .25in;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;9.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;Related Party Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;Related party transactions are provided in the normal course of business and, unless otherwise noted, are measured at the exchange amount, which is the amount of consideration established and agreed to by the related parties.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
